<p>Hi {{{Recovery__c.Contact_First_Name__c}}},</p>

<p>We wanted to let you know that we are unable to process your refund using the bank details you provided. You&#39;ll need to check your bank details and re-submit using our secure portal.</p>

<h3>How to organise your refund</h3>

<p>To process your refund, you will need to provide us with your bank account details using our secure case portal. If you&rsquo;re unsure about your bank details, you&rsquo;ll need to check with your bank before re-submission. Visit <a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/support/contact-us/customer-care-feedback-form/update-customer-care-case.html" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">https://www.qantas.com/au/en/support/contact-us/customer-care-feedback-form/update-customer-care-case.html</a> to update your details.<br />
<br />
All customers will receive email notifications about the progress of the claim. If you are a Qantas Frequent Flyer member, you can conveniently track your refund via the request tracker in the Qantas app via &lsquo;Track my cases&rsquo; in Help and Support.</p>

<h3>Need help?</h3>

<p>Call us on 13 13 13 (in Australia) or your local&nbsp;<a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/support/contact-us.html">Qantas Office</a>&nbsp;for assistance.</p>

<p>Have your Customer care reference number {{{Recovery__c.Parent_Case__c}}} ready to enter.</p>

<h3>If you&rsquo;re suspicious</h3>

<p>Not sure something is genuine? Remember, Qantas will never ask you to&nbsp;<u>email</u>&nbsp;your bank account details,&nbsp;credit card, PIN, or passwords.<br />
For more advice and warnings on scams please visit the Qantas scam assistance page -&nbsp;<a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/support/contact-us/scam-assistance.html" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">https://www.qantas.com/au/en/support/contact-us/scam-assistance.html</a></p>